{
  "name": "Graph Report — Auto Update",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "disabled": false,
  "description": "After each spec task completes, remind agent to update GRAPH_REPORT.md if the task changed project structure, dependencies, or state.",
  "when": {
    "type": "postTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "[GRAPH REPORT UPDATE] A task just completed. Evaluate if this task changed the project's structure in a way that GRAPH_REPORT.md should reflect (new files, new dependencies, new state keys, new services, changed data flow). If YES: 1) Read the current GRAPH_REPORT.md (or note it doesn't exist yet). 2) Read `~/.kiro/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` (the real graphify skill — it generates GRAPH_REPORT.md as one of its three outputs) and run `/graphify . --update` for an incremental rebuild instead of hand-editing sections. 3) Report: '📊 GRAPH_REPORT.md updated: [sections changed]'. If NO (task was a bug fix, test-only, config tweak, or documentation change that doesn't affect architecture): Report: '📊 GRAPH_REPORT.md: no structural changes — skipped.' If GRAPH_REPORT.md doesn't exist yet and the project now has enough structure to warrant one (3+ source files with dependencies): run the full pipeline via `/graphify .` per `~/.kiro/skills/graphify/SKILL.md` (no separate template needed — graphify generates GRAPH_REPORT.md itself). Report: '📊 GRAPH_REPORT.md created (initial generation).'"
  }
}
